    {
      "id": "cb_exemptions_and_review",
      "title": "Sovereign exemption, rebutted control, flagged dependence and credit protection",
      "category": "commercial_banks",
      "description": "Two PSUs controlled by the Government are not a group (sovereign exemption). A ring-fenced SPV's control link to its originator was rebutted to RBI, so they are not grouped. A suspected funding dependence between M and N is only flagged: the group breach it would cause is reported as POTENTIAL_BREACH for review. A guarantee from another bank moves part of Q's exposure to the guarantor. Exposure to the Government is exempt but still reportable.",
